The {{ nc.unresolved }} names without an NCBI node were queried again under all name classes and
synonyms. {{ nc.n_recovered | Words }} have a node under another name, and they are reported rather than linked
(Additional file 4). One shows why name-level links are not concept equivalence: NCBI files
*Bunodeopsis antilliensis*, which WoRMS accepts, as a name of *B. globulifera*. For
{{ nc.genus_absent | words }} of the unresolved names, NCBI holds no node for the genus either. Having a
node is not the same as having sequences: the {{ nc.linked }} linked taxa have a median of
